WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.570
Night, in a part of the castle
Harker was warned to avoid.

2
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:09.020
Moonlight, dust on the
floor, one set of footprints.

3
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.880
Three tall figures stand in
the moonlight, watching him.

4
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.770
A heartbeat speeds up.

5
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.390
Later, he writes down what he felt.

6
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.110
He is terrified.

7
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.420
And yet he lies still, and waits.

8
00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.490
Why?

9
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:28.800
In this mission, you'll learn how a Victorian
novel says what it cannot say outright.

10
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.310
You'll read the Chapter III scene closely,

11
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.190
in Harker's own words.

12
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.530
And you'll meet Lucy, changed,
in a churchyard at night.

13
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:41.080
Your mission: explain why Harker waits.
